From 41b9e3ac8e60f2bcfea207606ed32d2186b22831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YYH2913 <yyh2913@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 10:37:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] (pr-23990) wifi-scripts: set txpower per interface with ucode

The ucode mac80211 setup path applies the device txpower setting with
`iw phy <phy> set txpower ...`. On devices exposing multiple radios under
one wiphy this is a global setting, so setting up one radio can overwrite
the txpower selected for the other radios.

The legacy shell mac80211 script already applies txpower on every active
VIF with `iw dev <ifname> set txpower ...` after the interfaces have been
created and before reporting the wireless device as up, while only using
the wiphy level command when no radio suffix is in use.

Mirror that behaviour in the ucode implementation: keep the existing
wiphy-level command for non multi-radio devices, and apply txpower through
active interfaces when `config.radio` identifies a radio. Include OWE
transition BSS interfaces in the list so that all BSSes created for the
radio receive the same device txpower setting.

Use argv style `system()` calls for the new txpower commands so that
interface names are not parsed by a shell. Track configured, missing and
failed interfaces separately so secondary BSSes are not silently hidden by
a successful primary BSS update.

Some AP setup paths, for example DFS CAC, can apply channel state after the
initial interface setup. Schedule a bounded background retry after netifd is
notified that the device is up; the retry is token guarded so a later setup
run cancels older retry work without blocking the wireless handler.

This keeps per-radio txpower settings independent on single-wiphy
multi-radio devices.

Tested on an MT7996 single-wiphy 2G/5G/6G device with separate txpower
values for all three radios, including a DFS channel on 5 GHz.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
